I'm trying to avoid serious spoilers, but there may be a couple...

OK, so Eklavya the barbarian is making my deepest foray yet into the
DoD. Completed the Quest: the Thoth Amon proved elusive for a while by
scooting up the levels, until Eklavya thought of the simple trick of
level tporting one level up and descending upon the Thoth as he waited
at the foot of the stairs. What's more, he did all this on an
intelligence count of 10! Just wait till he gets to 25! A few loving
strokes from a Mjollnir and the Thoth was carrion fodder.

And I think the Heart of Ahriman is neato-keen! Until then I'd been
thinking of using a wish to get some boots to help me get around to the
back of the castle.

So, Eklavya cleans out the castle and picks up the wand. Never having
done this before, he gets himself a pet Archon. Ack! Turns out that
contrary to what I've been reading on r.g.h, the Archon doesn't hand
over his goodies to our hero! Maybe this is a 3.1.3 feature? However, he
is proving quite useful in Gehennom. But I'm *really* afraid of losing
him and having him turn on Eklavya with his Demonbane and his gaze.

Which brings me to my questions:

1) I stood outside and let the Archon dispose of my first priest of
Moloch. I'm wondering if it's a good idea now to convert the altar or
should I try not to annoy Moloch until absolutely necessary? In fact,
can you convert an altar in Gehennom to Crom at all? Is Crom going to be
any use at all henceforth? The only other time I entered Gehennom, Odin
didn't answer my prayer and let a perfectly splendid Valkyrie be done
in by some Vs. The reason I would want to convert is to make some holy
water. I'm afraid of losing my Archon if I scoot up many levels to find
an altar of Crom.

2) I have what it takes to escape inadvertently getting taken by level
teleporters, but is the Archon smart enough to avoid them?

3) I have a magic whistle, so I can keep my Archon close to me most
often, but how long can I stay away from him without him answering the
call of the wild? I find most traps, but if I step on a trapdoor, how
soon do I have to make it back up?

4) Can I put a leash on my Archon or will he take umbrage?

5) If, Crom forbid, my Archon should get lost, is he then susceptible
to charm?

6) Is there any way at all (in 3.1.3) to get him to drop Demonbane?
(I'd gladly give him Cleaver in exchange.) And that shield of
reflection he allegedly is wearing, according to what I've read?
(Incidentally, you'd think you could look at a monster and tell what
armour it's wearing, what weapons and wands it's carrying, etc. Why
doesn't nethack let you do that?)

7) This is the first time I used a ^L (I usually don't know anything
everyone else doesn't), did it work?
